# New (RESULTS.md, finding 1), reached with a kill (Milestone 305): 14 ms after the first swap
# acknowledged from step 20 on, a real-time relay in the guest kills the server before any of
# its threads runs on. The swap task is then between its two commits: the swapped index mapping
# is committed, its succeeded status is not. The restart runs the swap again, so sa and sb end
# as after an even number of swaps. The plain kill-meilisearch at the same delay passes. The
# moment moves with the image's bytes: on this image 13 ms gives it too.
# expect: violation      (change to ok when the bug is fixed)
disk=none | run A=meili.swap_acked@20+14:kill-now-meilisearch
